WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.863
- [Tricia] Do you know
who's hosting this year?

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.051
- Snoop Dogg?

00:00:05.051 --> 00:00:06.220
(triumphant music)

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.190
Okay, okay.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.299
So it's not.

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.540
- [Tricia] The city.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.570
- Oh, you mean like
hosting, like the person.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.180
I feel like Snoop Dogg
is hosting everything.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.597
So I'm like, so where do you think it is?

00:00:15.597 --> 00:00:16.430
- [Tricia] Beijing.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.960
I know it's in Beijing,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.560
so I was making sure that you knew.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.890
It was in Beijing.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.573
So, game begins now.

00:00:23.573 --> 00:00:26.260
(triumphant music)

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.093
Hey, what's up, y'all?

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.270
It is a big time of year for
us in the sporting community.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:35.110
I say us because obviously
I'm a 2021 Sports Emmy winner,

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.540
not once, but twice over.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.621
I won two.

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:39.583
We're Sports Emmy winners.

00:00:40.928 --> 00:00:43.290
Whether it was a mistake
or not, I earned it

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.680
and I'm keeping them and
I'm not changing the plates

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.520
even when you send me the
correct ones Emmy people.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.690
The 2022 Winter Olympics
are about to begin

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.580
on February 4th.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.270
Everybody in PSE can watch on NBC.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:55.570
You like that.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.430
There are so many different
Winter Olympic sports,

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:00.120
but there are also
apparently so many sports

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.370
that used to be, but are no
longer in the Winter Olympics.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:04.825
I don't know why they got kicked out.

00:01:04.825 --> 00:01:05.990
These are questions.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:07.780
So I'm being challenged to a game of,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.700
is this a Winter Olympic sport?

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.200
Let's see if I can guess them.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.460
Skeleton.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.713
Is Skeleton a winter sport?

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.253
Skeleton.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.410
I'm gonna say, no.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.510
How is Skeleton a winter sport?

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:27.865
I don't understand.

00:01:27.865 --> 00:01:29.226
(buzzing noise)

00:01:29.226 --> 00:01:30.059
Oh, it is.

00:01:30.059 --> 00:01:30.892
Skeleton is a...

00:01:30.892 --> 00:01:32.523
You felt good about your er.

00:01:33.772 --> 00:01:35.563
You're wrong.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.870
It's not in the script, I just enjoy it.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.547
Skeleton is a Winter Olympic sport.

00:01:39.547 --> 00:01:40.380
(ding)

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.213
Oh, I remember that.

00:01:41.213 --> 00:01:43.150
I didn't know that's what that was called.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.010
Skeleton is a current Winter Olympic sport

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:49.330
where a competitor rides
face-first down a frozen track

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.078
on a small sled known
as a skeleton bobsled.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.980
Did not actually know the name of it,

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.620
but yes I do know this.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.453
This always scares me.

00:01:58.453 --> 00:02:00.080
This is like nightmares of like,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.547
even in like elementary
school, people are like,

00:02:01.547 --> 00:02:02.667
"I'm gonna go down the slide head first."

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.710
I'm like, "Why would you do that?"

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.191
Like, I feel like you're
going to break your neck.

00:02:07.191 --> 00:02:10.420
Why risk it for a playground fun time?

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:13.090
Like I don't get it, but
people do what they do.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.363
Skeleton is a sport.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:16.629
A current one.

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:18.810
(triumphant drum beat)

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.403
Icicle Javelin.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.650
I don't think Icicle Javelin is a sport,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.190
but I really want it to be.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.983
Like a big giant javelin.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.624
I feel like this is a sport in
Frozen, in the movie, Frozen.

00:02:33.624 --> 00:02:35.315
This is not a real sport.

00:02:35.315 --> 00:02:36.148
(bell chiming)

00:02:36.148 --> 00:02:39.010
Yeah, Icicle Javelin is
not a Winter Olympic sport,

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.740
but wouldn't it be fun?

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.400
(dramatic music)

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.030
Oh, Skijoring.

00:02:47.108 --> 00:02:48.428
Skijoring.

00:02:48.428 --> 00:02:51.468
Is Skijoring a Winter Olympic sport?

00:02:51.468 --> 00:02:52.917
I don't even know what the hell it is.

00:02:52.917 --> 00:02:54.058
Skijoring.

00:02:54.058 --> 00:02:54.891
Skiing

00:02:56.291 --> 00:02:57.124
Joring

00:02:57.124 --> 00:02:57.957
I don't know.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.230
I'm going to say, yes.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.063
I'm gonna think Ski...

00:03:01.063 --> 00:03:06.063
Maybe you're skiing and you're
trying to go through rings or

00:03:06.077 --> 00:03:07.740
you're trying to aim for rings.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.760
I don't know.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.610
I don't know what it is.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.077
I feel like I won the game of BS.

00:03:11.077 --> 00:03:11.910
(bell chiming)

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.920
It is a former Winter Olympic sport.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.345
Let's find out more.

00:03:15.345 --> 00:03:16.760
(ding)

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.437
Oh, Skijoring is where a human on skis

00:03:20.437 --> 00:03:23.156
is pulled by a galloping horse.

00:03:23.156 --> 00:03:25.140
Skijoring was held solely at the

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.790
St. Moritz 1928 Winter Olympic Games.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:33.370
That just seems like a lot of work.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.860
I feel like that's why they got rid of it.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.190
I'm really glad that's not one.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.830
It seems weird, but also kind of miss it

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.105
because that'd be really fun.

00:03:39.105 --> 00:03:40.065
- [Cowboy] Heehaw.

00:03:40.065 --> 00:03:40.898
- And look at that cowboy.

00:03:40.898 --> 00:03:43.120
He's like, come on.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.313
I feel like this is what
people on ranches do

00:03:45.313 --> 00:03:47.710
when they get just hammered.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.505
And they're like, "I have
this really great idea.

00:03:49.505 --> 00:03:51.399
I'm gonna pull you behind the horse."

00:03:51.399 --> 00:03:54.202
(neighing horse)

00:03:54.202 --> 00:03:55.970
(upbeat music)

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.010
Ski Ballet.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.310
Is Ski Ballet a Winter Olympic sport?

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.110
I feel like you're going
to break your ankle.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.240
That's like a dumb thing.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.670
I feel like you slip and
fall and snow and ice.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.666
Like why would Ski Ballet be a sport?

00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:11.327
I'm going to say, no.

00:04:11.327 --> 00:04:12.855
(buzzing sound)

00:04:12.855 --> 00:04:13.688
(ding)

00:04:13.688 --> 00:04:16.695
Oh, Ski Ballet is a former Winter Olympic.

00:04:16.695 --> 00:04:21.060
Ski Ballet is a mixture of
figure skating and skiing.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.440
Performing a two-minute
ballet-like routine

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.313
outdoors on skis.

00:04:25.313 --> 00:04:26.179
On skis?

00:04:26.179 --> 00:04:29.777
Demonstrated at the '88 and
'92 Winter Olympic games.

00:04:29.777 --> 00:04:31.740
Well, it's probably not a thing anymore

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:32.950
because people are so confused.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.143
I'm still confused by it.

00:04:35.143 --> 00:04:36.060
Oh, my God.

00:04:37.451 --> 00:04:41.102
(up tempo disco music)

00:04:41.102 --> 00:04:42.280
Oh, my God.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.493
Look how joyful.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.073
Oh, my gosh.

00:04:47.241 --> 00:04:48.640
That guy, he is like

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.990
♪ Fame, I'm gonna live forever ♪

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.823
That's amazing.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.210
Oh, my God, that guy.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.683
I'm going to picture him all day today.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.770
(epic music)

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.400
Ice Sculpting.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.833
Is competitive Ice Sculpting
a Winter Olympic sport?

00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:06.730
If it's not, it should be.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:07.720
I love sculptures.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.830
I think it's the most amazing
thing to be able to do that.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.100
I think that Ice Sculpting
should be if it's not,

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:13.933
I'm going to say, yes.

00:05:13.933 --> 00:05:14.862
(buzzing sound)

00:05:14.862 --> 00:05:15.695
Ah, it isn't.

00:05:15.695 --> 00:05:16.700
(ding)

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:17.930
It's an art form.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.460
I mean, you got to be strong to do it.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.480
- [Tricia] What would you sculpt?

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.610
- What would I sculpt?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.041
You.

00:05:23.041 --> 00:05:25.070
(melodic music)

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.430
Trisha Farrow.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.650
I would just sculpt her.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.800
Ice Sculpting is not a
Winter Olympic sport.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.410
Although people do compete in it.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.403
Okay, so it's not, but it should be.

00:05:34.312 --> 00:05:36.090
(dramatic music)

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.360
- Whoa, Biathlon?

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.193
Biathlon.

00:05:39.193 --> 00:05:42.160
Is Biathlon a Winter Olympic sport?

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:42.993
Biathlon.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.410
What the hell is Biathlon?

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.530
Biathlon, hmm.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:49.913
I'm gonna say,

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:52.673
okay, Biathlon,

00:05:52.673 --> 00:05:54.830
so it's like a bunch of things, maybe.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.090
If it is something because
it's like a triathlon.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.790
Like, you know, like athlon,

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.940
I feel like it's maybe,

00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:03.600
I'm going to say, no.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.013
I'm going to say Biathlon is
not a Winter Olympic sport.

00:06:06.013 --> 00:06:06.846
(buzzing sound)

00:06:06.846 --> 00:06:09.533
- [Tricia] I just like that
you're like a triathlon.

00:06:10.422 --> 00:06:12.090
Bi would be two.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.282
- I know, but like what...

00:06:13.282 --> 00:06:14.893
I know, that's what I was saying.

00:06:14.893 --> 00:06:16.490
Wait, well, that's what I was saying

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:17.323
because like a triathlon.

00:06:17.323 --> 00:06:19.560
So I thought maybe, but then I
was like, when is a biathlon?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.530
What would they be doing?

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:23.110
The biathlon is a race that combines

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.671
cross-country skiing and rifle shooting.

00:06:25.671 --> 00:06:29.550
Once again, is this a real thing still?

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.870
- [Tricia] Yes.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.103
- I'm gonna watch this.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.570
You know what'd be cooler,

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.143
it wasn't rifle shooting,
it was bow and arrow.

00:06:39.138 --> 00:06:42.138
(upbeat epic music)

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.950
Oh, Kase Essen.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.835
Kase Essen.

00:06:47.835 --> 00:06:49.774
That was my German, Yurman.

00:06:49.774 --> 00:06:52.880
Is Kase Essen a Winter Olympic sport?

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:56.940
I mean, first of all, what
the hell does Kase Essen mean?

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.510
So, I don't know.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:00.081
I'm going to say, sure. Yeah.

00:07:00.081 --> 00:07:00.914
(buzzing sound)

00:07:00.914 --> 00:07:01.747
Oh, nope, it is not.

00:07:01.747 --> 00:07:03.010
It is not a Winter Olympic sport.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.432
What is it?

00:07:04.432 --> 00:07:08.323
Kase Essen is just
German for eating cheese.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:11.995
Oh, it's good.

00:07:11.995 --> 00:07:13.350
I like cheese.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:15.420
That's the end of the game.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.880
I wasn't very good at it, but anyway,

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.590
good luck to everybody
in the Winter Olympics.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.250
It's such a cool thing for
the family to sit around

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.627
and watch together.

00:07:22.627 --> 00:07:24.150
Thank you for working so hard.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.640
I know it's probably weird circumstances

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:26.840
that y'all are under because everybody is

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.090
because of, you know, the pandemic.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.860
So thank you for all your hard work.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.790
Thank you for entertaining us

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:35.090
and congratulations on
being an Olympic athlete.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.400
- [Tricia] If you were to ever
compete in Winter Olympics,

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.640
what sport would you be good at?

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.163
- Oh, eating cheese, Kase Essen.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.976
I will be eating some
cheese and enjoying a

00:07:46.976 --> 00:07:49.820
(speaking French) with some pinot noir

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.674
while watching you be athletic.

00:07:51.674 --> 00:07:55.424
(triumphant music plays out)

